^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-11-13 12:00] observe — Both mounted consumers pin 9ef3d223, six commits behind main. Two prereleases are cut (2026.11.13-pre.1 at e664081f, pre.2 at 3f9e933e); no day is. The story consumer committed five times since yesterday evening (releases 2026_11_12.A and 2026_11_13.A, finds, live gift obstacles and a module split of its game, and at 11:17 a direction cache for workbench agents). Its audio frame asks for configurable earcons on container open and close, a dwell aura, and user profiles, and asks for a schema that retunes them in under three lines of Spw. Its parser bundle exports only parse and readBias.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:00] decide — Tonight's release answers that ask and nothing wider: one line of Spw for the earcon settings, and enter and exit events for a caret. Editor extensions, stereo shaping and capsule clicks wait.
 >>[2026-11-13 13:10] decide — The owner asked to commit first; the plan landed alone, then this slice. Earcons live in their own module (earcons.ts) so pair-sound keeps one reason to change. The words are the parser's names for the three pairs (body, frame, scene), ms for a click's length, rough[off] for no rough tone; a binding reads as a bracket does (body: 392). The changelog is one dated section in this commit rather than its own.
 >>[2026-11-13 13:30] surprise — The round-trip law caught writeEarcons rounding to three decimals and comparing rounded values, so a setting near its default (rough 1.414 against 1.41421…) was not written and read back as the default. Numbers are now written exactly.
 >>[2026-11-13 13:40] verify — 12 tests on earcons: every setting from one line, a binding and a line laid over three lines read alike, every number clamped and reported, unknown, unusable and repeated words reported, a written line reads back to the same settings for 300 generated settings, and the line a host would offer tunes the clicks pairSound makes; pairMoves holds order, reversal, silence inside a pair, the close as inside, and agrees with a brute-force count over 300 generated texts. Four mutants (moves not innermost first, no clamp, unknown words dropped, write-all ignored) each fail a test; the last needed a test of its own. Seed 1,165 pass, LSP 405, CLI 419, runtime 137, DOM 3, parser release 24, tsc clean. spw quest's walk test now has a 30 s limit. Nothing was heard.
}

